some secrets about my playing style: I try to get lvl1 spellbooks asap
and identify them by price, don't bother with the rest but sell them
unidentified. apart from the very usefull lvl1 spells (sleep, detect
monsters, light, healing,...) I go for identify and remove curse. in
the past about half of my YASDs have been stupid ones because I had in
my inverntory the means to save me but either had no identify scrolls
or was trying to save them for later.

getting the casting chance for indetify below 50% is one of the first
goals. GoD, HoB are essential for this. opposed to many other players I
go with the rule: 'rust/fire/corrosionproof first, enchant later' on
important gear. later I have other things to do but searching for
!oConf and rustproofing. I rather have a rustproof +3 HoB in midgame
than a very rusty +5 one.

protection: asap getting them by eating stuff (if not monk anyway).
don't bother with rings. =oslowdisg. and =oconfl. are too important.
amulets: LifeSaving lets you make a mistake and try again - that
feature is build into NetHack already ;-) so don't bother. reflection
is the thing. major demons: breaking 2 wands of create monster and then
casting charm monster or just wearing =oconfl. or summoning hordes of
gas spored then teleporting out without you pet are my preferred way to
deal with them.

